comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T05:46:55.259Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status 2658-item title/metadata catalog and source ledger reviewed; current query act r activation nearest pm-doxj,pm-4k6b,pm-rnpb,pm-92if,pm-n7rr. No individual owner for this experiment was found. Shared scorer/signal/packer baselines are prerequisites, not proof of this distinct mechanism. User requested individual planning records; this draft preserves the open cognitive-architecture decision gate and does not accept the ADR. Estimate is a one-day initial spike budget, not a delivery forecast."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T06:11:52.282Z","harness:codex","Activation experiment constraint: elapsed times are positive durations relative to a pinned observation boundary. Define the zero-access prior, simultaneous-event convention and clock-skew handling before evaluating logarithmic power-law activation. The historical decay exponent is a hypothesis; do not claim that a human-memory model proves optimal project-context retrieval over minutes through decades. Compare against maintenance-invariant semantic recency and event-quantile recency, with no future events leaking into training labels."
body: "## Proposal and provenance\n\nStable algorithm slug: `act-r-activation`. Source: pm-4k6b note recorded 2026-07-07T15:12:12.161Z.\n\n(1) Scale-free recency via ACT-R base-level activation: activation(i) = ln(sum over accesses t_j of t_j^-d), d~0.5, computed from the item's history stream timestamps. Log-time decay is the one law that behaves identically for a minutes-old scratch workspace and a decades-old archive (the spectrum invariant pm-z436/pm-g2zz demand) and it rewards frequency AND recency in one term, replacing ad-hoc half-life constants.\n\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nEvaluate this mechanism as a bounded public-SDK experiment before any production adoption. Use the existing scorer and packer contracts; no CLI-only behavior or new command noun. The historical catalog is design input, not evidence that this mechanism was implemented.\n\n## Experiment protocol\n\nFreeze a workspace/history revision and parameter manifest. Compare against the current deterministic SDK baseline using held-out judgments and negative controls. Report nDCG/action success, critical-evidence omission, latency p50/p95, peak memory, tokens per completed task, and rebuild cost separately. Include 3-item/minutes, real-shaped, 100k/1M-item, decades-long, and sparse/dense/imbalanced graph scenarios; smoke subsets may not claim scale acceptance. Bound candidate counts, graph expansions, elapsed time, and output size, with cancellation and completeness receipts. Record exact versus approximate behavior and approximation error; theoretical guarantees require their stated assumptions. Missing or untrusted evidence remains unknown, never inferred proof.\n\nPromotion requires a reproducible quality improvement on the held-out target population, no regression of existing exact invariants or mandatory gates, and a declared compute/token cost justified by that improvement. Reject or defer with the same immutable evidence if those conditions fail. No production default, adaptive learning, or data export is authorized by this planning item."
